See `AGENTS.md` in the repo root for the canonical guide. CLAUDE.md and
.cursorrules are also symlinks to AGENTS.md — keep the single source.

Key rules every agent must follow:

1. Every MCP tool runs through `withTimeout` — declare in
   `ToolDefinition.timeoutMs` or rely on the default.
2. `noteActivity()` fires on every dispatch (feeds the idle watchdog).
3. Wrap a `perf()` span around every handler.
4. Errors get an actionable hint + tool name via `wrapToolError`.
5. Honor `AbortSignal` in long-running loops.
6. NEVER `console.log` after `StdioServerTransport.connect()` — JSON-RPC
   owns stdout. Log via `@george43g/robustness/logger`.
7. Sanitize user-content surfaces with `sanitize()`. Wrap external
   content with `wrapUntrusted()`. UUID-gate any embedded instructions.

After any change:
- `pnpm build`
- Restart the MCP host so it picks up the dev proxy's reloaded child.
- Call the relevant `mcp__browser-tab-mcp-dev__*` tool to confirm the
  change works end-to-end.
- `pnpm test` (or `pnpm verify` for the full suite).
- `pnpm stress` if the change touches dispatcher / lifecycle / transport.
